#. English reference: Why does LexiShield require a password for its vaults?
msgid "help.pwd_h4"
msgstr ""

#. English reference: LexiShield was engineered to protect enterprise-grade secrets and highly confidential personal data. A password is mandatory for three non-negotiable architectural reasons:
msgid "help.pwd_p1"
msgstr ""

#. English reference: Fundamental principle: Zero-Knowledge architecture
msgid "help.pwd_principle"
msgstr ""

#. English reference: Immunity to physical or forensic attacks: if someone accesses your hard drive, without the master password it is mathematically impossible to reconstruct the link between protected values and real secrets.
msgid "help.pwd_r1"
msgstr ""

#. English reference: Argon2id + ChaCha20-Poly1305 cryptography: the decryption key is never stored in any file; it is derived via memory-hard Argon2id parameters to neutralize GPU and ASIC brute-force attacks.
msgid "help.pwd_r2"
msgstr ""

#. English reference: Strict per-project or per-client isolation: by assigning different passwords to different vaults (.lexi), you guarantee an impenetrable cryptographic wall for each client or environment.
msgid "help.pwd_r3"
msgstr ""

